<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:scilab="http://www.scilab.org"  xml:lang="en" xml:id="grayplot">
    <refnamediv>
        <refname>grayplot</refname>
        <refpurpose>2D plot of a surface using
            colors
        </refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>grayplot(x,y,z,[strf,rect,nax])
            grayplot(x,y,z,&lt;opt_args&gt;)
            h = grayplot(...)
        </synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection role="arguments">
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>x, y, z</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        Real matrices defining the grid and the surface values : 
                                <literal>x</literal> and 
                                <literal>y</literal> can be row vectors of sizes n1 and n2 and <literal>z</literal> a real matrix of size (n1,n2)
                                (rectangular grid) or the 3 matrices can have the same size (n1,n2) (curvilinear grid).
                            </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>&lt;opt_args&gt;</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        This represents a sequence of statements <literal>key1=value1,
                            key2=value2
                        </literal>
                        ,... where <literal>key1</literal>,
                        <literal>key2,...</literal> can be one of the following: rect, nax, strf, logflag
                        or axesflag and frameflag (see <literal>plot2d</literal>).
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>strf,rect,nax</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        see <literal>plot2d</literal>.
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>h</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>This optional output contains a handle to a Grayplot entity. Use <literal>h</literal> to modify its properties.
                      For a list of properties, see <link linkend="grayplot_properties">grayplot_properties</link>.
                    </para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para>
            <literal>grayplot</literal> makes a 2D pseudo-color plot of the surface <literal>z</literal>
            on the grid defined by <literal>x</literal> and <literal>y</literal>. Each cell of the grid
            is filled with a gray or color level depending on the average value of <literal>z</literal>
            at its corners. If <literal>z</literal> contains <literal>%nan</literal> values, the
            surrounding cells are not displayed.
            When <literal>x</literal> and <literal>y</literal> are vectors the grid is rectangular;
            when <literal>x</literal>, <literal>y</literal> and <literal>z</literal> are all matrices
            of the same size the grid is non-rectangular, with node (i,j) located at
            <literal>(x(i,j), y(i,j))</literal> — useful for curvilinear or polar coordinates.
        </para>
        <para>
            Enter the command <literal>grayplot()</literal> to see a demo.
        </para>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
x=-10:10;
y=-10:10;
m=rand(21,21);
grayplot(x,y,m,rect=[-20,-20,20,20])
 ]]></programlisting>
        <scilab:image>
            x=-10:10;
            y=-10:10;
            m=rand(21,21);
            grayplot(x,y,m,rect=[-20,-20,20,20])
        </scilab:image>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
t=-%pi:0.1:%pi;
m=sin(t)'*cos(t);
clf()
grayplot(t,t,m)
 ]]></programlisting>
        <scilab:image>
            t=-%pi:0.1:%pi;
            m=sin(t)'*cos(t);
            clf()
            grayplot(t,t,m)

        </scilab:image>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
// Non-rectangular grid: sector of an annulus in polar coordinates
[R,T] = ndgrid(linspace(0.1,1,100), linspace(0,%pi/4,50));
grayplot(R.*cos(T), R.*sin(T), rand(T))
 ]]></programlisting>
        <scilab:image>
            [R,T] = ndgrid(linspace(0.1,1,100), linspace(0,%pi/4,50));
            grayplot(R.*cos(T), R.*sin(T), rand(T))
        </scilab:image>
    </refsection>
